1
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:05,980
=The Cruel Tribunal=
=Episode 9=

2
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,100
Why did she jump
into the river with her child?

3
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:14,000
Whoever marries a wife like this

4
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:14,920
is unlucky.

5
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:16,600
It's just life.

6
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:18,280
What was so hard to get over?

7
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:20,200
Isn't this just causing
trouble for her family?

8
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:21,120
Exactly.

9
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:23,480
What fault could
the child possibly have?

10
00:01:28,020 --> 00:01:29,500
Just because she couldn't have a son?

11
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:56,000
This is not your fault.

12
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:07,200
This is not your fault either.

13
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:11,440
This is not your fault.

14
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:14,680
Miss Xiaobai.

15
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:16,120
Wait a moment.

16
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:23,920
What happened here?

17
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:25,400
They jumped into the river.

18
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:49,880
This way, you won't get lost from Mother.

19
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:01,960
He Dang,

20
00:03:02,630 --> 00:03:03,720
go find the mortuary workers

21
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:04,880
and give them a proper burial.

22
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:06,240
Yes.

23
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,440
So unlucky.

24
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:37,600
Wang Wen, stop right there.

25
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:45,040
You come with me.

26
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:47,200
Who do you think you are
to tell me to go with you?

27
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,840
Today, I'll show you who I am.

28
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,840
(Zhaoming Office)
Silence.

29
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:54,120
Silence.

30
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:56,640
Official Huang,

31
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:58,690
are you going to pass
judgment on this case or not?

32
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,400
Advocate Jiang,

33
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,160
Wang Wen

34
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:08,400
didn't steal,

35
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,080
nor did he rob.

36
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,040
He committed no crimes,

37
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:12,680
and besides,

38
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:14,200
the people at the docks

39
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,440
can all testify

40
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:18,440
that Qiniang indeed
threw herself into the river.

41
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:19,400
I...

42
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:20,640
Sir.

43
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,040
Sir, you are wise.

44
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,480
I was so unlucky

45
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:27,200
to marry such a wife.

46
00:04:27,210 --> 00:04:27,760
It's really...

47
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:30,290
It really brought ruin and
financial loss upon my family.

48
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:34,200
Dare you say it again!

49
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,440
Go on, speak.

50
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:37,160
Weren't you so talkative just now?

51
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:39,080
Sir...

52
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:40,520
Advocate Jiang,

53
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:41,080
calm down.

54
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:42,280
Calm down.

55
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:44,280
After all, we are in an official court.

56
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:45,360
Let's talk about facts

57
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,760
and reason through this.

58
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,080
Fine.

59
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:49,320
An official court,

60
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:50,520
reasoning through facts.

61
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,480
Wang Wen pawned his own wife,

62
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:53,840
agreeing on the amount,

63
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:55,120
the duration, and the purpose.

64
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:57,000
Do you also believe

65
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:58,880
that a woman is an object to be traded?

66
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:00,080
Well...

67
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:01,360
In the Eastern Market of the city,

68
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:02,880
the pawn value of an ox

69
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:04,160
costs 20 taels of silver.

70
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:05,720
Yet Wang Wen pawned his own wife

71
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:07,280
for a mere ten taels of silver.

72
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:08,000
Official Huang,

73
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:09,280
a human being

74
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:10,400
is somehow worth less than livestock.

75
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:11,680
Is this your justice?

76
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:13,860
It is true that Qiniang
took her own life in the river,

77
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:15,800
but if they hadn't
pushed her to the brink,

78
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,280
how could she have come to this?

79
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:19,880
Fine.

80
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:21,920
Official Huang,

81
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,320
if I don't touch him now

82
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:28,720
and simply force Wang Wen
to jump into the river,

83
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:29,720
does that mean

84
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,120
it doesn't count as murder either?

85
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:32,920
Sir.

86
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:33,880
Sir...

87
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,520
Save me, sir.

88
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:40,500
- Advocate Jiang, calm down.
- Sir.

89
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:42,080
Calm down.

90
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,400
Pawning one's wife

91
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,080
is permitted

92
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:48,120
by the laws of the dynasty.

93
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,560
In this matter,

94
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:50,680
I

95
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:52,880
cannot rule in your favor.

96
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:02,960
Sir.

97
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:05,520
Wang Wen,

98
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:08,360
you owe Chen Pi 20 taels of silver,

99
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,720
with three days remaining.

100
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,800
If you fail to repay it on time,

101
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,240
I will punish you

102
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,280
with forced labor service.

103
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:14,990
Do you understand?

104
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:15,880
I understand.

105
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:17,120
I understand, sir.

106
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,400
Court is adjourned.

107
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,080
Thank you, sir.

108
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:25,280
Thank you, sir.

109
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:39,480
(I am determined to overthrow)

110
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:40,880
(this man-eating system.)

111
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:46,100
(Bright Mirror Hangs High)

112
00:07:55,860 --> 00:08:00,300
(Zhaoming Office)

113
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:03,120
Miss Xiaobai,

114
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:04,640
have something to eat first.

115
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,080
Miss Xiaobai...

116
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:24,920
Advocate Jiang.

117
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:26,880
Advocate Jiang,

118
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:27,880
stop beating it.

119
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:30,520
Stop beating it.

120
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,120
Stop beating it.

121
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:34,440
Advocate Jiang,

122
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:36,480
even if you break this grievance drum,

123
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:38,000
nothing will come of it.

124
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:39,480
According to

125
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:41,080
the current dynasty's laws,

126
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,920
this case of Wang Wen and Qiniang

127
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,720
really has no grounds for a verdict.

128
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,400
Are you saying, Official Huang,

129
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:49,560
that this is the only way?

130
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:52,520
There is another way.

131
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:53,420
Appeal directly to the Emperor.

132
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,120
However, to appeal directly
to the Emperor,

133
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:54,880
you must undergo

134
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,320
the pain of corporal punishment.

135
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:00,400
Could I ask you

136
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:01,400
to do me a favor?

137
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:03,000
What favor?

138
00:09:03,190 --> 00:09:04,590
Under the old custom of pawning wives,

139
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,480
(Zhaoming Office)
there are thousands of victimized women.

140
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:08,760
I want to investigate
all past cases thoroughly.

141
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:24,200
Your Highness.

142
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:33,680
Yunsheng,

143
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,040
do you miss home?

144
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:36,720
Yes.

145
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,120
I miss my mother,

146
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:41,800
my betrothed wife,

147
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,480
and the old locust tree

148
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,560
in front of my house.

149
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:46,320
If you could go back,

150
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,390
what would you want to do most?

151
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:49,520
Get married

152
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:51,320
and have a child.

153
00:09:59,120 --> 00:09:59,920
Are you scared?

154
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:01,320
No.

155
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:03,440
With Your Highness here,

156
00:10:03,450 --> 00:10:04,800
what do I have to be afraid of?

157
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,520
I'll go ladle a bowl of soup for you.

158
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:16,680
(Xiaobai,)

159
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:19,800
(are you doing well?)

160
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:25,140
(Archives Repository)

161
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:29,760
Official Huang,

162
00:10:30,190 --> 00:10:31,680
it's been a while since we last met.

163
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:33,640
I just happened

164
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:35,240
to be here to look into something.

165
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,240
This legal clerk

166
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:38,720
looks a bit unfamiliar.

167
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:39,600
And

168
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:41,240
why does he look so young?

169
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:44,000
You remember Clerk Niu, right?

170
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:46,360
He's been sick in bed
the last couple of days.

171
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:47,440
Isn't it a coincidence?

172
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:49,040
This lad from my relative's family

173
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:50,480
came from my hometown recently

174
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,120
to look for work with me.

175
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:57,120
Why are you being so rude?

176
00:10:57,120 --> 00:10:58,920
Say hello when you meet a stranger.

177
00:10:58,920 --> 00:10:59,440
Quick,

178
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:00,440
greet Scribe Zhang.

179
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,200
Scribe Zhang.

180
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:04,720
Since he's family,

181
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,890
there's no need to be so polite.

182
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:07,480
It's his first time meeting me,

183
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:08,440
so he's shy.

184
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:09,680
Yes, exactly.

185
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:11,960
He ate something bad these days
and got an upset stomach,

186
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:12,990
so he doesn't look too well.

187
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:14,600
We'll head in first then.

188
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,760
See you later.

189
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:17,590
Go on with your work.

190
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:18,920
Let's go.

191
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:20,000
Eat less in the future.

192
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:21,080
Eating so much every day...

193
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:38,400
Where did this woman come from?

194
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,160
Whose lady is that?

195
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:43,600
Liu,

196
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:45,360
that's my eldest nephew.

197
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:48,080
A few days ago, while castrating a pig,

198
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:50,280
he accidentally got
kicked in the throat by the pig.

199
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:52,920
Luckily,

200
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,400
it only kicked his throat.

201
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:55,320
Otherwise,

202
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:57,760
it would be a waste
of his handsome looks.

203
00:11:57,770 --> 00:11:59,660
I'm afraid no matchmaker
would fancy him then.

204
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:01,080
Yes, indeed.

205
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:02,480
He's fine now.

206
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:03,440
Go on with your work.

207
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:11,360
Don't make random noises, please?

208
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,920
You're taking the law
into your own hands, huh?

209
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:14,520
Let me tell you,

210
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:16,760
you're impersonating
a public official right now.

211
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,520
If you get caught,

212
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:20,790
you know what happens, right?

213
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:24,320
You've been searching for so long,

214
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,520
have you found it yet?

215
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:31,420
(Archives Repository)

216
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:39,860
(Zi'an County Pawned Wife Case Memorial)

217
00:12:40,540 --> 00:12:45,060
(Pawning and Selling the Principal Wife)

218
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,240
Official Huang,

219
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:51,520
I found it.

220
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:54,700
(Zi'an County Pawned Wife Case Memorial)

221
00:12:57,500 --> 00:13:00,100
♪The candle burns down
to its final glow♪

222
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:03,460
♪Cold fragrance clings to my hem♪

223
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:05,860
♪You gently smooth my hair♪

224
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:08,780
♪Yet your gaze drifts far away♪

225
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:13,660
♪A hidden blade lies beneath your smile♪

226
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:17,340
♪You turn away
as if nothing has changed♪

227
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:19,500
♪Step by step, I walk away♪

228
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:22,980
♪Each step breaks my heart anew♪

229
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:28,620
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

230
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:32,220
♪Why leave me
standing alone in the wind?♪

231
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:35,260
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

232
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:39,300
♪Yet all that's left
is warmth upon my fingertips♪

233
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:42,580
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

234
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:45,660
♪And write of every meeting
and every parting♪

235
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:48,380
♪If next life asks
about the days gone by♪

236
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:51,620
♪I'll only say that once♪

237
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,860
♪I called your name♪

238
00:13:58,460 --> 00:14:00,700
♪The silent stars hang low♪

239
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:04,300
♪The river keeps flowing east♪

240
00:14:05,540 --> 00:14:07,460
♪I linger in the old tower♪

241
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:11,220
♪Waiting for you,
though all is now empty♪

242
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,980
♪This life still owes us a bow♪

243
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:18,660
♪May the next repay us with a dream♪

244
00:14:19,420 --> 00:14:21,660
♪Beyond here lie
endless mountains and rivers♪

245
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:27,900
♪I dare not turn for one last look♪

246
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:31,060
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

247
00:14:31,660 --> 00:14:35,140
♪Why bury this heart beneath the frost?♪

248
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:37,780
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

249
00:14:37,780 --> 00:14:42,060
♪Now only fading warmth
remains in my palm♪

250
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:44,980
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

251
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:48,140
♪And paint a winter between your brows♪

252
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:50,820
♪If we meet again in another life♪

253
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:53,860
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

254
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:56,820
♪Was when we first met?♪

255
00:14:58,100 --> 00:15:00,500
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

256
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:03,380
♪Was when we met for the last time?♪
